Error [E0070]: this uses a retired arrow spelling
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3202_ptr_boundary.jet:3:21
    |
  3 |     fn return_ptr() => *Int = "DemoReturnPtr";
    |                     ^^
 Why: callables, arms, and lambdas use one arrow: `->`
 Fix: replace `:>` or `=>` with `->`

Error [E0068]: This callable uses the retired result-arrow shape.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3202_ptr_boundary.jet:3:21
    |
  3 |     fn return_ptr() => *Int = "DemoReturnPtr";
    |                     ^^
 Why: a return type sits after the parameter list, and `->` introduces the body; an effect ceiling follows the return type
 Fix: write `fn name(...) Type -> body`, or `fn name(...) Type -[Effects]> { … }`

Error [E3202]: Type `*Int` cannot cross the C boundary here.
  --> tests/ui/cffi_e3202_ptr_boundary.jet:3:24
    |
  3 |     fn return_ptr() => *Int = "DemoReturnPtr";
    |                        ^^^^
 Why: C FFI allows by-value scalars and `String` in ordinary code; pointers and other gated types need `use core.mem` and an `#Unsafe { … }` region (S58).
 Fix: Move the call inside `#Unsafe`, or change the type to a C-safe value type.
